    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41307" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rescīssōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id.; cf. rescissio; in jurid. Lat., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to abrogating</i>, <i>revoking</i>,
			or <i>rescinding</i>, <i>rescissory</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">actio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					4, 6, 28 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			— As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rescissōrĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., = rescissoria actio, <i><span class="en">Dig. 39,
				5, 21</span></i>.</div>
